{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T21:27:16.727Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"3079dc08a6d576f9312fe4ba","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T21:27:16.727Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Expanded canonical corpus includes combined variable/function indirection: ship() { NPM=npm; $NPM \"$@\"; } hides publishing from the pinned auditor. Variables resolving to alias, eval and builtin eval also hide alias-created publishing. The consumer rejects unknown arguments on variable-routed commands and variable-routed aliases/evaluators using canonical tokenization of literal leading bindings as rejection evidence only. A literal npm dist-tag named eval and a literal array-looking argument remain accepted controls."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T21:27:16.727Z"}],"before_hash":"05d6a4c802aa83ca164a679810e32648462e863cc33b3f8c94e501ab64d4b8bc","after_hash":"97f957c5bad6e33931c1092a7994f1456a29382c76ed16d22ce1475e653b7d2b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a37ac4d721e06766909e8c46979806f03b64dd211046ecc1ab78c627ed3156d0"}
